# Build context is kotlin/. Keep local build output out of the sandbox image.
#
# Without this, `COPY decouple-monolith/` bakes in exercise/bin/ and solution/bin/,
# which Gradle and the IDE fill with a second copy of every .kt file. Those copies
# are stale the moment you edit src/, so the image carries two versions of the same
# TODO comments. Verified present in a built image.
#
# The leading **/ is load-bearing. A bare `bin/` matches only <context>/bin, NOT
# decouple-monolith/exercise/bin, so the first version of this file silently did
# nothing. Verified: `bin/` alone still shipped bin/ in the image.
#
# The Dockerfile compiles both trees itself, so nothing here is needed at build time.
**/bin/
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.idea/
**/*.iml
**/.DS_Store
